.TH CREATE\-NETWORK\-TSHOOT\-LIVECD 8 "2026-08-19" "1.0.0" "Network Tools"
.SH NAME
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \- build a standalone, boot\-only live ISO for
NIC cabling diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd
.B \-c
.I CSV
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd
builds a distro\-independent, hybrid (UEFI+BIOS)
.BR live\-build (7)
ISO for boot\-only NIC cabling diagnostics.
Unlike
.BR nic\-xray (8),
it is a standalone tool: it does not clone a PVE template, does not depend
on the Proxmox VE tool stack, libguestfs, or
.BR rear (8),
and it never writes to any attached block device on a normal boot.
.PP
On boot the ISO will:
.IP 1. 4
Read the system serial number (DMI) and look it up in the CSV (embedded in
the image, or an override copy read from a labelled partition on the boot
media) to set the hostname and, optionally, a bonded VLAN management IP.
The hostname is always applied on a serial match, independent of whether
network parameters are supplied.
.IP 2. 4
Bring up every physical NIC, then start
.BR lldpd (8)
for neighbour discovery once link bring\-up (including any bond/VLAN
enslavement) has settled, so freshly learned neighbours are not discarded
by the link bounce.
.IP 3. 4
Automatically run
.B nic\-xray \-\-all \-\-output csv
and render a human per\-NIC table (interface, link state, MAC, speed,
LLDP neighbour) to
.B both
the VGA console and every auto\-discovered serial console.
.IP 4. 4
Drop to an interactive root shell with
.BR nic\-xray ,
.BR lldpcli (8),
and
.BR tcpdump (8)
on
.BR PATH .
.PP
No disk write occurs on a normal boot: the kernel command line disables
GPT auto\-activation and swap auto\-on
.RI ( systemd.gpt_auto=0 ,
.IR rd.systemd.gpt_auto=0 ,
.IR noswap ),
and the report/CSV are written only to a
.B tmpfs
.RI ( /run/tshoot/cabling\-report.txt ).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Required
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-csv " " \fIFILE\fR
Host inventory CSV file, embedded into the ISO at build time.
See
.B CSV FORMAT
below.
.SS Image base
.TP
.BI \-\-base " debian|ubuntu"
Live\-image base distribution.
Default:
.BR debian .
.TP
.BI \-\-dist " VERSION"
Release of the chosen base.
Default:
.B 13
for
.BR debian ,
.B 24.04
for
.BR ubuntu .
Determines which exact\-match OBS tree
.RB ( Debian_13 ", " Ubuntu_24.04 ", " \.\.\. )
.B nic\-xray
is pulled from.
.SS Target network (applied on boot, per host)
Per\-host IP and bond members come from the CSV; these parameters define
how the shared management interface is constructed (bond \(-> VLAN \(->
IP assignment).
Network configuration is optional \(em omitting it still yields hostname
identification, NIC bring\-up, and the LLDP/nic\-xray report.
.TP
.BI \-\-bond\-mode " MODE"
Bonding mode.
Default:
.BR 802.3ad .
.TP
.BI \-\-vlan\-id " ID"
Management VLAN ID.
Default: no VLAN.
.TP
.BI \-\-netmask " MASK"
Network mask (e.g.
.BR /24 " or " 255.255.255.0 ).
Required when
.B \-\-gateway
or
.B \-\-dns
is specified.
.TP
.BI \-\-gateway " GW"
Default gateway.
Required when
.B \-\-netmask
or
.B \-\-dns
is specified.
.TP
.BI \-\-dns " SERVERS"
Comma\-separated list of DNS servers.
Required when
.B \-\-netmask
or
.B \-\-gateway
is specified.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " URL"
HTTP/HTTPS proxy made available inside the live environment.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.BI \-\-lldp\-wait " SEC"
Seconds to poll
.B lldpcli show neighbors
for non\-empty output before giving up and rendering the table as\-is
(timed from the last NIC link\-up).
Default:
.BR 45 .
.TP
.B \-\-include\-switch\-xray
Also install the sibling
.B switch\-xray
package for switch\-side diagnostics from the shell.
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory for the ISO file.
Default: current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-build
Retain the generated
.BR live\-build (7)
configuration tree and chroot after the build (success or failure) for
inspection.
Default: cleaned up automatically.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built\-in help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.SH CSV FORMAT
The host inventory file is a comma\-separated file with four columns, the
same format used by
.BR pve\-create\-tshoot\-image (8):
.PP
.RS
.nf
# serial,hostname,bond_members,ip
SVR001,web\-server\-01,eth0:eth1,10.0.0.11
SVR002,db\-server\-01,eno1:eno2,10.0.0.12
SVR003,app\-server\-01,ens1f0:ens1f1,10.0.0.13
.fi
.RE
.PP
.TP
.B serial
DMI system serial number (matched at boot).
.TP
.B hostname
Hostname to assign.
.TP
.B bond_members
Colon\-separated list of NIC names to bond (e.g.
.IR eth0:eth1 ).
The colon separator allows different hardware across servers.
If a listed name does not exist under the live image's NIC naming policy,
detected interface names are printed alongside the warning to aid the
operator.
.TP
.B ip
Management IP address.
Optional \(em omit the column value to identify the host by hostname only.
.PP
Lines beginning with
.B #
are treated as comments.
.PP
The CSV baked into the ISO can be overridden at boot time without a
rebuild: if a labelled partition on the boot media (e.g. a second
partition on the USB stick) carries a replacement CSV, it takes
precedence over the embedded copy; otherwise the embedded copy is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
Minimal build, hostname identification and cabling report only:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \-c hosts.csv
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build to a specific output directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \-c hosts.csv \-o /var/tmp/iso/
.fi
.RE
.PP
With a bonded VLAN management network:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \-c hosts.csv \e
    \-\-vlan\-id 100 \-\-netmask /24 \e
    \-\-gateway 10.0.0.1 \-\-dns 8.8.8.8
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ubuntu 24.04 base with a longer LLDP settle window and switch\-side tools:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \-c hosts.csv \e
    \-\-base ubuntu \-\-dist 24.04 \e
    \-\-lldp\-wait 90 \-\-include\-switch\-xray
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep the build tree for troubleshooting a failed
.BR live\-build (7)
run:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-create\-tshoot\-livecd \-c hosts.csv \-\-keep\-build
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/tmp/tshoot\-livecd\-*/
Temporary
.BR live\-build (7)
configuration tree and chroot created during the build.
Cleaned up automatically on success unless
.B \-\-keep\-build
is given; retained on failure for inspection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (missing dependencies, unreachable package repository, build
error, etc.).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.SS Build host
.BR lb (1)
(the
.B live\-build
package),
.BR debootstrap (8),
.BR xorriso (1).
No Proxmox VE tools, libguestfs, or
.BR rear (8)
are required \(em the tool runs on any Debian\- or Ubuntu\-based build host.
.SS Package source
.B nic\-xray
(and, with
.BR \-\-include\-switch\-xray ,
.BR switch\-xray )
are pulled at build time from the openSUSE Build Service project
.B home:ciriarte:network\-tools
, which publishes exact\-match apt trees for
.BR Debian_12 ", " Debian_13 ", " Ubuntu_22.04 ", and " Ubuntu_24.04 .
Both packages are
.B Architecture: all
(noarch, script\-based), so any of the supported bases is an exact match
with no ABI coupling.
The repository signing key is fetched over TLS and used with the
.B signed\-by
keyring mechanism; the build fails closed if the key or the matching tree
is unreachable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nic\-xray (8),
.BR live\-build (7),
.BR lldpd (8),
.BR lldpcli (8),
.BR tcpdump (8)
